            <ArticleTitle>[Progresses on adverse health effects of automobile exhaust].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>504-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The progresses on the latest studies at home and abroad on adverse health effects of automobile exhaust were reviewed in this paper. Particulates and poisonous gases from automobile exhaust were considered to be harmful to respiratory system, immune system and reproductive system. It showed that increased prevalence of respiratory disease (e.g. chronic bronchitis and asthma), and decreased lung function, immunity were associated with automobile exhaust. The carcinogenic potential from the exposure to automobile exhausts needs to be further explored because the carcinogenesis is multifactorial.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
